{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Orchestrator close — acceptance criteria ticked on the implementing agent's REPORTED per-AC\nevidence, and the change is merged to `origin/main`.\n\nWhat I verified myself before ticking:\n- the merge commit exists on `origin/main` and carries this ticket's `rebar-ticket:` trailer;\n- the commit is reachable from a throwaway worktree checked out at `origin/main`, which is where\n  this close is being run (the shared main checkout holds another session's uncommitted work, so\n  it was deliberately not fast-forwarded);\n- both Gerrit gates were green on the submitted patchset (`LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`).\n\nWhat I did NOT independently re-run: the per-AC commands. Those were executed and their output\npasted by the implementing agent, and CI re-ran the full suite on the patchset. Recording the\ndistinction so the trail says which evidence is first-hand and which is relayed — the completion\nverifier gate is the independent check on the criteria themselves."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788589551029485001,"uuid":"8cf003da-4688-40d7-ab5a-eae084d7b529"}